welcome to the tempest this scoutship  is sleek stealthy and with its ability  to cover 13 lightyears in a day  incredibly speedy let's take a quick  tour the meeting room is where you can  make vid calls or summon the crew for a  powwow as you can see it's also the  place to go for stunning panoramic views  of whatever part of the galaxy you're  currently occupying head down a floor to  reach the research room and it's to  auxilary rooms the bio lab and tech lab  you'll spend a lot of time here between  missions tinkering with the R&amp;D terminal  as the name suggests this is where  you'll research new weapons armor and  accessories using research data gathered  during missions and then develop them  using accumulated minerals and omni gel  and if you fancy you can rename your  development projects however you see fin  like so these are your personal quarters  where you can pick up side quests  coordinate outfits and entertain your  crewmates feel free to abuse your  position by making terrible fashion  choices safe in the knowledge that your  crew will never call you on them talking  of whom here's where they get to sleep  it's a little let's say cozier than your  quarters but still worth a visit to  check out the crew info board to see  what your crew gets up to between  missions just over the other side you'll  find the medical bay home to the respect  station this is where you can reallocate  skill points for you and your crew  albeit at a price take a trip down to  the cargo bay if you'd like to check out  the engine core this imposing orb is  based on the same technology as the  Ark's Odyssey Drive hence its ability to  navigate the galaxy at such impressive  speeds finally there's the bridge where  you can chat with Silurian pilot callo  jeff and science officer su v Anwar  slightly more importantly it's home to a  console that lets you set the course for  your next journey and in true Mass  Effect's fashion scan planets and  asteroids for valuable minerals the  now you know your way around the tempest  it's time to get out there and start  exploring  good luck Pathfinder
 

